asn't and  we actually had to go and get the test  ourselves from the hospital  to test that person to make sure that  they weren't um  uh positive by the time we got the test  we subsequently found they were positive  and they were being readmitted back  and unfortunately passed away um yes it  was dreadful we were worried because we  saw the nhs  um was dealing with a very difficult  issue they had ppe  we didn't and was reassuring our staff  and our residents that we knew was  happening and doing the best  we possibly could it was frightening um  and  if it weren't for the hard work of  social care staff and in fact the local  authorities in our area  they would those figures i'm i'm  confident would have been much much  worse  mr cummings said this week that um  when matt hancock uh had put said he'd  put a shield around care homes  he was telling untruths  um somebody is not telling the truth  here  uh hancock says he wasn't lying  um who do you think was telling the  truth well i can only give it as i see  it and i don't want to accuse  uh i weren't there to who to hear who  said what to whom  all i would say is i don't believe  myself there was a ring of protection  thrown  around us in those very early days um it  was  difficult we were forgotten we've been  forgotten over decades  that's the only issue in social care we  weren't prepared we weren't um ready we  didn't have the pp we didn't have the  testing  and it took the government many many  weeks to actually see what was happening  in homes  despite our best efforts and process  stations that's why providers  i think without their efforts the  figures as i said just now would be it  would have been much worse so  they take some credit particularly the  staff of course  of course there was a crisis in social  care before covid  and there is a crisis in social care now  and unless we do something about it  there will probably be a crisis in  social care  in the future what do we need to do now  well it's